vault-not-made = That folder could not be made a vault
no-music-folder = No primary folder is chosen. Press the circle beside a folder to make it the one new songs are kept in.
primary-note = The primary folder is where songs dragged onto the window are copied, with their covers and lyrics, each checked against its original. It is scanned like the others, so what lands in it joins the library.
make-primary-hint = Make this the primary folder: the one new songs are kept in
primary-hint = The primary folder, where new songs are kept. Press to choose none.
primary-badge = Primary
clear-primary-hint = Choose no primary folder. The folder is left alone.
music-folder-gone = This folder is not there now. If it is on a drive, mount it before adding songs.
in-the-vault = That folder is inside the vault, which keeps its own objects. Choose a folder outside it.
not-a-folder = That is not a folder
no-folder-picker = Couldn't open the folder picker; type the folder instead
forget-hint = Forget this folder and every track scanned from it. The files are left alone.
forget-asked = Press again to forget this folder, its tracks, and the plays, favourites and details kept for them.
forget-asked-label = Press again to forget
no-folders = No folders yet. Add one and Resonate will scan it; press its circle to make it the primary folder.
folders-note = Everything under these folders is read into the library and followed while the window is open. The files are only read: nothing in them changes unless Tagging or Organising below is applied.
files-note = Rescan reads what was added or changed since the last scan. Read every file again re-reads each file whatever its size and time say: names, lengths, cue sheets, covers and the search index. Plays, favourites and playlists are kept.
resuming-note = The queue comes back paused on the row it was playing, so nothing starts on its own. Files named on the command line are queued instead of what was kept.
forever = Forever
five-years = Five years
two-years = Two years
a-year = A year
six-months = Six months
a-while = A while
every-listen-is-kept-so-the = Every listen is kept, so the statistics can reach back to the first one.
lookup-under-way = The lookup so far
last-lookup = The last lookup
details-note = Look up asks MusicBrainz about the albums and artists not asked lately, which a scan does on its own when Online allows it. Refresh all asks about everything again. Look for missing covers asks the archive again for every album with no picture. Speed up once lets this lookup study the songs on every core but one with no rest between them, until it ends; MusicBrainz is still asked at its own pace.
template-label = Where each track is filed
organising-note = Each / is a folder under the music folder the track was scanned from. Preview lists what would move; only Apply moves anything, and the catalog follows the files.
moved-under-the-preview = The catalog moved since the last preview, so it was taken down. Preview again to see what would happen now.
preview-first = Preview first, so what would move is on screen before anything does.
ask-again-to-move = Press it again to move the files. Nothing is copied — every track is renamed where it stands.
ask-again-to-put-the-tags-back = Press it again to put back what the last run wrote into every file it wrote: each field as it read before, a cover it added taken out and the rating it changed restored.
ask-again-to-put-back = Press it again to put every file the last run moved back where it stood. Putting it back twice files them again.
tagging-note = Writes what a lookup answered for back into the files themselves, so another player reads the same names. Only fields the catalog was told about are touched, and a cover goes in only where the file carries none.
preview-tags-first = Preview first, so what would be written is on screen before anything is.
ask-again-to-write = Press it again to write the files. Each one is read back afterwards, and what does not read back is not followed.
nothing-to-tag = Nothing to write. Every scanned file already says what the catalog was told about it.
cover-art = cover art
file-dropped-songs-by-the-layout = File dropped songs by the layout
off-they-keep-the-names-and = Off, they keep the names and folders they came with
add-folder = Add folder…
scanning = Scanning…
rescan-folders = Rescan folders
read-every-file-again = Read every file again
look-for-missing-covers = Look for missing covers
stopping = Stopping…
stop = Stop
looking-up = Looking up…
look-up = Look up
sped-up = Sped up
speed-up-once = Speed up once
refresh-all = Refresh all
add = Add
the-last-lookup-was-stopped-early = The last lookup was stopped early
carry-the-queue-over = Carry the queue over
off-every-run-opens-on-an = Off, every run opens on an empty queue
keep-what-was-listened-to = Keep what was listened to
a-skip-repeats-the-queue = A skip repeats the queue
off-a-skip-goes-on-repeating = Off, a skip goes on repeating the track it lands on
how-shuffle-orders-the-queue = How shuffle orders the queue
spread-each-artist-apart = Spread each artist apart
songs-by-one-artist-are-heard = Songs by one artist are heard across the queue rather than in a cluster
spread-each-album-apart = Spread each album apart
songs-from-one-album-are-kept = Songs from one album are kept apart too, within an artist as well
songs-heard-this-week-come-last = Songs heard this week come last
what-you-have-not-heard-lately = What you have not heard lately is played before what you have
previous-restarts-the-song = Previous restarts the song
off-previous-always-goes-back-a = Off, previous always goes back a track
previewing = Previewing…
preview = Preview
moving = Moving…
press-again-to-move-the-files = Press again to move the files
apply = Apply
press-again-to-put-them-back = Press again to put them back
put-the-last-run-back = Put the last run back
file-the-tracks-that-way = file the tracks that way
use-that-layout = use that layout
writing = Writing…
press-again-to-write-the-files = Press again to write the files
vault-note = Decodes every scanned track the vault does not hold, throws its tags and its pictures away, keeps the smallest bit-exact copy it can make and points the catalog at it. The files it read are left exactly where they are.
no-vault = No vault is open. Choose the folder it should keep what it imports in; an empty folder becomes one.
vault-at-the-next-start = Opened from the next start, and what is imported from then on is kept there.
in-the-library = That folder is inside a library folder, which would scan the vault's objects as songs. Choose a folder outside every one.
preview-import-first = Preview first, so what would be kept is on screen before anything is.
ask-again-to-keep = Press it again to keep the tracks. Nothing the vault reads is moved, renamed or written to.
nothing-to-keep = Nothing to import. The vault already holds every scanned track it can.
choose-folder = Choose folder…
keeping = Keeping…
press-again-to-keep-the-tracks = Press again to keep the tracks
no-inbox = No inbox is named, so nothing can fill a want. Choose the folder the files arrive in.
inbox-note = A file directly inside it named by the recording's MusicBrainz id, the track's or the ISRC fills the want it names. The folder is read and never written to.
choose = Choose
polling = Polling…
poll-now = Poll now
random = Random
smart = Smart
by-album = By album
every-song-in-the-queue-in = Every song in the queue in any order, as a die would have it.
every-song-in-the-queue-laid = Every song in the queue, laid out so the same artist or album does not come round again soon, as the switches below say. A song the library does not hold is placed at random.
whole-albums-one-after-another-each = Whole albums one after another, each in its own order, the albums in any order. Turned on mid-album, the album playing plays on first.
days-kept = { $days } days
listens-older-than-forgotten = Listens older than { $days } days are forgotten as the library opens, once ListenBrainz has been told of them.
folder-is-not-a-folder = { $folder } is not a folder
folder-to-add = { $folder } to add
folder-to-forget = { $folder } to forget
waiting-for-the-pass = Waiting for the pass under way to finish: { $waiting }
lookup-ended-early = The last lookup ended early: MusicBrainz couldn't be reached while looking up { $asked }
scan-counted = discovered { $discovered } · read { $read } · added { $added } · updated { $updated } · moved { $moved } · removed { $removed } · failed { $failed }
press-again-to-forget-listens = Press { $label } again to forget every listen older than that now, for good. Listens ListenBrainz has not been told of yet are kept until it has.
and-more = and { $rest } more
retag-so-far = already said { $unchanged } · passed over { $passed_over } · walked { $walked }
retag-written-so-far = written { $written } · already said { $unchanged } · passed over { $passed_over } · walked { $walked }
retag-previewed = would write { $writes } · fields { $fields } · pictures { $pictures } · ratings { $ratings } · already said { $unchanged } · passed over { $passed_over } · nothing has been written
organise-so-far = in place { $unchanged } · unidentified { $unidentified } · collided { $collided } · failed { $failed }
organise-moved-so-far = moved { $moved } · in place { $unchanged } · unidentified { $unidentified } · collided { $collided } · failed { $failed }
organise-previewed = would move { $moving } · in place { $unchanged } · unidentified { $unidentified } · collided { $collided } · failed { $failed } · folders to empty { $folders } · nothing has moved
stopped-before-it-finished = { $told } · stopped before it finished
kept-again = { $form } again
vault-previewed = would keep { $walked } · nothing has been written
inbox-asked = asked { $asked } · kept { $kept } · not kept { $unkept } · nothing { $nothing } · refused { $refused } · late { $late }
